theory.intro:
**Resolving** a vector means splitting it into two perpendicular parts. Every vector is the sum of a horizontal part $x\underset{\sim}{i}$ and a vertical part $y\underset{\sim}{j}$. From a magnitude $r$ and an angle $\theta$, $x=r\cos\theta$ and $y=r\sin\theta$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,angles,quotes,calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (3.6,2.7);
\coordinate (Q) at (3.6,0);
\coordinate (E) at (4.6,0);
\draw[dashed] (O)--(Q) node[midway,below]{$x=r\cos\theta$};
\draw[->] (Q)--(4.9,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[dashed] (Q)--(P) node[midway,right]{$y=r\sin\theta$};
\draw[-{Stealth},thick] (O)--(P) node[midway,above left]{$r$};
\coordinate (r1) at ($(Q)!0.3cm!(O)$);
\coordinate (r2) at ($(Q)!0.3cm!(P)$);
\draw (r1)--($(r1)+(r2)-(Q)$)--(r2);
\pic[draw, "$\theta$", angle radius=0.9cm, angle eccentricity=1.8] {angle = E--O--P};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
Write the vector $\underset{\sim}{a}$ shown below in component form.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.55]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[step=1,gray!25,very thin] (-5,-1) grid (5,6);
\draw[->] (-5.4,0)--(5.4,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.4)--(0,6.4) node[above]{$y$};
\foreach \i in {-4,-2,2,4} \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\i,0){$\i$};
\foreach \i in {2,4,6} \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,\i){$\i$};
\draw[-{Stealth},thick,blue] (0,0)--(-3,5) node[above left]{$\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Write the vector $\underset{\sim}{b}$ shown below in component form.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.55]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[step=1,gray!25,very thin] (-1,-6) grid (7,2);
\draw[->] (-1.4,0)--(7.4,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-6.4)--(0,2.4) node[above]{$y$};
\foreach \i in {2,4,6} \node[above,font=\scriptsize] at (\i,0){$\i$};
\foreach \i in {-2,-4,-6} \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,\i){$\i$};
\draw[-{Stealth},thick,blue] (0,0)--(6,-5) node[below right]{$\underset{\sim}{b}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
A wind blows at $40$ km/h on a true bearing of $060^{\circ}$, as shown. Resolve the wind velocity into exact east and north components.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.5]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta, angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Npt) at (0,2.6);
\coordinate (W) at (30:2);
\draw[->] (-1.6,0) -- (2.4,0) node[right] {$E$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.6) -- (Npt) node[above] {$N$};
\draw[-{Stealth},thick] (O) -- (W) node[above right] {$40$ km/h};
\pic[draw, "$60^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.8cm, angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle = W--O--Npt};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

Write the vector shown below in component form, with each component correct to one decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,angles,quotes,calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (3.064,2.571);
\coordinate (E) at (4.2,0);
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(4.4,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.5)--(0,3.2) node[above]{$y$};
\draw[-{Stealth},thick] (O)--(P) node[midway,above left]{$14$};
\pic[draw, "$40^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.9cm, angle eccentricity=1.8] {angle = E--O--P};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
